{"id": "EUVD-2025-206584", "enisaUuid": "57bd9d17-6a8a-3938-b253-ee4d1841c7e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: at_hdmac: fix device leak on of_dma_xlate()\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken when looking up the DMA platform\ndevice during of_dma_xlate() when releasing channel resources.\n\nNote that commit 3832b78b3ec2 (\"dmaengine: at_hdmac: add missing\nput_device() call in at_dma_xlate()\") fixed the leak in a couple of\nerror paths but the reference is still leaking on successful allocation.", "datePublished": "2026-01-31T11:42:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:11:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49d964cde422dc66fea514b7ab24aa729df7081d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c67b4f45c8540ee4e62e24ca4608c6a9a81ee0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48b2d7f530b83cb149dbf0e48f95ccadb2d90da9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/987c71671367f42460689b78244d7b894c50999a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a86cf2c09e149d5718a5b7090545f7566da9334", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3c23b7e941349505c3d40de2cc0acd93d9ac057", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9074b2d7a230b6e28caa23165e9d8bc0677d333"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4c95-wpmq-cc75", "CVE-2025-71191"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "160dd307-b770-34e7-85e0-bab639ddb6ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.162"}, {"id": "38e81f39-3e7b-3663-8652-da0adda2f782", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.249"}, {"id": "3c889a98-0288-3f49-989a-f230001794df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.199"}, {"id": "3ee8c757-c898-3e87-82a6-5293c76f1d5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bbe89c8e3d598129b728d1388c3ad9abe4e8e261 <49d964cde422dc66fea514b7ab24aa729df7081d"}, {"id": "529eae2f-d9ce-3e6c-